# internal/util/inspect   const call = Function.prototype.call; function inspect(value) { return call }  exports = { inspect }
# main                    printed[Symbol.for("nodejs.util.inspect.custom")] = custom; console.log(printed)
# The program asks for no module of the library: native code requires the start-up module on its own, so the body of the module is no seen code.
# Its read names the evaluator all the same and answers it, as the operation `Builtin` does there: what hangs from `Function` is followed. A read is no event.
# evaluator-called-in-function-of-library-that-only-native-code-enters.ir has the call of an evaluator in such code
